# A build of an add-on reads the ignore file beside its Dockerfile (<Dockerfile>.dockerignore), which lets in only the
# kit and that add-on. This file covers a builder that does not read those files: it keeps secrets, local stores,
# binaries and the modules the images do not build out of the context.
**/bin
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/kubeconfig*
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.db.lock
**/*.test
*/kind
cma/livecheck
